  "result": "Done! I've implemented customer statements:\n\n**Created src/statements.js:**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` \u2014 generates a customer statement showing unpaid invoices\n  - Validates customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)\n  - Filters for invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n  - Filters for issueDate on or before asOf date\n  - Returns `{ customerId, invoices, totalDue }`\n  - Each statement invoice includes: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n    - `due` calculated via `balanceDue()` from payments.js\n    - `total` calculated via `invoiceTotals()` from invoices.js\n  - Invoices sorted by issueDate (earliest first)\n  - `totalDue` = sum of all `due` amounts\n\n**Created test/statements.test.js:**\n- 13 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - Empty and null invoice lists\n  - Filtering by status (includes issued/partially_paid, excludes draft/paid)\n  - Filtering by asOf date\n  - Correct sorting by issueDate\n  - Correct totalDue calculation with multiple invoices\n  - Customer filtering\n  - Unknown customer rejection\n  - All required fields in statement output\n- All 169 tests pass\n\n**Design:**\n- Statement is a snapshot of a customer's outstanding invoices as of a specific date\n- Excludes draft invoices (not yet issued) and paid invoices (no balance due)\n- Useful for billing inquiries, collection activities, and accounts receivable",
